From 207dedbade0ce86ca07e5699538306c4da231116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:43:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the lobby through the game's own menus (SRNP_LOBBY=2,
 experimental)

Gibax's design: each player chooses in the game's own Player Entry (the host also in Track Select and
Rule Settings), then a waiting screen with everyone's choice, then the race. The runner starts free:
its game runs alone (no lockstep) with the player's pad on port 0, two B presses bring Player Entry back
to the character choice. When the player presses Start, the menu sets the race up (the racer count
leaves 1): racer 0's character and gear (+0xBA, +0xBB: the menu writes the gear there, 0 being each
character's own board) go to the relay (PICK, READY), the host's course and laps too (RULES), and the
waiting screen shows until GO (the host may still set the racers, Z). At GO every runner loads its start
state again (on another thread: State::LoadAs waits for the CPU to stop), notices it back (the racer
count is 1 again), writes the rules, counts the game frames from 1 and starts the lockstep as from the
boot; seat 0 presses Start (frame 10). The waiting screen stays over the running game (a before-present
hook) until 15 frames after that Start has set the race up, so the start state's Player Entry is never
seen; at GO it shows everyone ready ("EVERYONE READY!").
Measured: 2 runners with simulated presses (Sonic; right right A A Start: Knuckles) and Gibax with his
pad (Sonic on gear 7 against Knuckles): the choices read from the menus, both runners load the start
state again and race them; 19 and 104 identical checksums, 0 divergence. The start state's path comes
from the runtime (SetStartState).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
